        <body>
            <div xml:id="d291">

                <pb facs="0334" n="264" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg264"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/2651</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the French Chargé</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chambrun</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-24">December 24,
                            1918</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of a Note from the French Ambassador, dated November 12, 1918, advising
                    that the Minister of Foreign Affairs of the French Republic states that the
                    delegate of the Polish National Committee at Paris, recognized by the Allies,
                    has applied to him for permission to participate in the peace conference when
                    questions bearing upon Polish affairs are taken up, and requesting to be
                    informed as to the sentiment of the United States government on the subject.</p>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to say that as soon as the position of the United
                    States on this question is determined you will be promptly informed.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank L. Polk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
